# server/predictor-data snapshots are SHA-256-verified byte-for-byte against
# MANIFEST.json (server/predictor/store.js) at load time. Git line-ending
# conversion (core.autocrlf / eol attributes) would silently change the bytes
# between platforms and break those hash checks in whichever environment
# converts. Treat the whole store as byte-exact: no eol conversion anywhere,
# working tree always equals the committed blob.
server/predictor-data/** -text
